xt player has [B2,B3,B4] \u2014 **B3 was just used in a Chi by the next player**! So B3 is **very dangerous** \u2014 do NOT discard.\n- **Play W2 / W1 / T1**: All terminals or edges. W1 and T1 are 1s \u2014 possible components of terminals/honors or knitted patterns. But again, previous player discarded W1 \u2014 maybe safe.\n- **Play F2**: South Wind. Across player discarded F2 twice, next player discarded once \u2014 likely safe. Less risky than F1.\n\nBest options: **Play F1**, **Play F2**, or **Play W9**\n\nReason:  \nB3 is extremely dangerous due to recent Chi action ([B2,B3,B4]) by the next player. Avoid discarding B3 at all costs.  \nW1, W2, T1, W9 are terminals \u2014 possible draws for outside hands or all terminals, but limited use otherwise.  \nF1 and F2 are both non-prevalent/non-seat winds (we are North), so less valuable. Since F2 has been discarded more frequently (across and next players), it's safer to play.  \nDiscarding **F2** minimizes risk while progressing toward a Melded Hand (if you win off a discard). It also keeps slightly better balance in honors.\n\nAnswer: Play F2"}
